From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:10:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] Scale to the panel on request: V4L2_REQUEST_SCALE=panel

The H713's decode-time scaler (cedrus with the local kernel patches,
negotiated by V4L2_REQUEST_SCALE=WxH since the patch "Negotiate the H713
decode-time scaler") needs a size per board and per clip. The value
"panel" lets the driver choose it: the panel is the first DRM connector
in /sys/class/drm that is connected and enabled, its first mode the
native size (HY310 card1-LVDS-1 1920x1080). A frame larger than the
panel by more than 64 lines or columns decodes to the largest even size
of its own shape that fits (3840x2160 on 1920x1080 -> 1920x1080,
3840x1600 -> 1920x800); anything else decodes as before, unscaled. The
slack keeps padded streams of panel size as they are: 1080p H.264 is
coded 1920x1088 and must not be squeezed by eight rows. The shape is
V4L2_REQUEST_CROP's when the client gives the visible size, otherwise
the coded frame's. The same choice is made for surfaces exported before
their first decode, so a client that keeps those fds gets the layout the
decoder writes. V4L2_REQUEST_SCALE=WxH behaves exactly as before.

It is not the default, and cannot be, on purpose: VA-API has no way to
tell a client that a surface holds a smaller picture than the client
created it for, and the clients import at the size they believe in.
mpv 0.40 sizes its EGL images from the frame (dmabuf_interop_gl.c,
EGL_WIDTH/EGL_HEIGHT from the image params, not from the descriptor),
Kodi 21 from the picture (VaapiEGL.cpp, CVaapi2Texture::Map,
DVDPic.iWidth/iHeight), GStreamer va from its caps. Panfrost rejects a
3840-wide import of a 1920-pitch buffer: measured on the HY310 with
mpv --hwdec=vaapi --vo=gpu under cage and a 4K H.264 and HEVC clip,
every frame failed with "Failed to import surface in EGL: 12291"
(EGL_BAD_ALLOC) and the wall stayed black, where the same clips without
scaling play. Turned on for every client it would make every 4K video
black. A client that imports at the size the export descriptor reports
(width/height of VADRMPRIMESurfaceDescriptor, the real geometry since
"Report the surface's own size in exports") can set it.

License: GPL-3.0-or-later, like the code it changes (libva-v4l2_request).
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
